n:
The final scenes of the new heaven and earth show a new community and home for God's people, created and given by God. These scenes uplift persecuted Christians. John shares his main vision ({{Revelation 21:1-8|Revelation 21:1–8}}) and expands on it in two parts: 

- In {{Revelation 21:9-27|Revelation 21:9–27}}, he describes the new Jerusalem as a place of holy perfection;

- in {{Revelation 22:1-5|Revelation 22:1–5}}, he portrays the new Jerusalem as the ultimate garden of Eden, which Adam and Eve could have experienced if they had not sinned.
